WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:03.140
Apparently, Yano was going out with a girl two grades above him...

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.230
So he likes older girls...

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.810
How long were they going out?

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.690
From the end of his 2nd year to the summer of the 3rd.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.030
The rumors came out of nowhere and spread like wildfire.
Only half a year? That's short.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:11.990
Isn't that long?

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.820
Right now, I'm having a really hard time.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.240
Yamamoto-san!

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.740
You're well enough to be running in gym again?

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:19.370
Yeah.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:23.750
Oh, I got a 34 on the last math test!

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.460
I'm finally free of that zero!

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.750
I guess next time you'll have to get higher than a 56.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.380
You'll fail if your average is under 30, right?

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.800
What? Really?

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.840
I-I'll try my best!

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:43.390
Yano is still the same as ever...

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.610
No way! They don't look alike at all!

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:18.280
Seriously, they really don't.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:19.450
What are you guys talking about?
Seriously, they really don't.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:20.950
The Asahi Middle School yearbook.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:22.950
Yamamoto-san's older sister is in here.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.240
You know, the one Yano was going out with!

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.000
Nana, come take a look!

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.290
Ah, I'll... pass...

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.840
Hey, anyone have change for a 5,000 yen bill?

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.220
I dooooon't!

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:38.880
Okay...

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.890
Hey, anyone?

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.140
Anyone have change for 5,000 yen?

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.350
Yano just doesn't change...

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.190
I guess it's to be expected.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.600
Since we met, Yano's just been like that.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.190
I guess I just don't know anything about him yet...

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:55.940
Bye bye!

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.360
That committee meeting lasted longer than I expected...

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.300
What class was she in again...?

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.010
Class 3-5.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.060
I'm sorry, Yano...

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.150
I was just curious...

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:33.730
This must look pretty bad.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:38.860
Show me that.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.660
I still haven't looked at it myself.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.330
Wanna see?

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.210
Not really!

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.010
I guess I do!

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:05.850
Though I didn't want to see it under these circumstances...

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:09.680
Since I don't know what kind of expression to--

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:14.230
He only goes for pretty faces!

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.150
S-She's really pretty, isn't she?

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.860
Yeah, but this is nothing. In person, she's even prettier.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.780
I-It's over...

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.410
I've completely lost to her.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:29.620
She doesn't really... resemble Yamamoto-san, huh?

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.750
I guess not.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.250
Which one of you fell for the other first?

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.750
Me. It was love at first sight.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.460
So you started dating right away?

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:43.050
No, it took a while. She had a boyfriend at the time.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.050
Did you steal her away?

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:44.880
That's right!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.930
Er, are you trying to make me look bad?

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:51.560
What is it?

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.890
Nothing...

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:58.480
I've just never seen Yano so fixated on one thing before...

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.650
You must have loved to brag about her, huh?

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:06.410
She was my first. The first I'd ever really loved.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:14.210
My chest hurt, but since Yano smiled as he talked, it quickly settled down.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.750
I probably didn't want to accept it...

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.420
The existence of someone Yano loved...

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:31.560
Yano, I...

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.600
I think I might like you...

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.400
Just ignore me! I just wanted to try sayin--

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.690
Then, wanna go out?

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:48.030
H-Huh? W-Wait a sec...

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.070
You really like me back?

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:52.950
Yeah.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.120
W-Wait a second! You hesitated!

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:56.830
Did not.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.460
Did too! You definitely did!

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.460
Forget it!

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:00.290
No.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:02.710
Do you really like me?

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.710
Yeah, I guess.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.300
Not that sort of "like".

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.300
I'm asking if you really, really like me.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.020
I'm sorry... I don't know.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.270
What's up with that...?

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.020
Then, let's just forget it.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.440
I don't want something like that.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.110
If we're going to go out, I want you to like me back...

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:29.740
Okay.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.370
"Okay"?

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.410
Even though it was the first confession I'd made since I was born...

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:44.420
...to get a quick and painfully honest "okay" as an answer...

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:50.340
I wonder if I should've pretended to not hear him and said "yeah"...

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:54.430
Yano.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.980
You were sound asleep.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.270
What? Can't you do it?

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:03.190
That's unusual.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.690
Yamamoto, show me you can fill in the rest.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.440
Yano, you stay here and watch.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.590
Yano? Yano.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.970
What's the matter? You look pale.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:33.890
Yano!

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.390
Here. Take this.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:38.100
It's good against anemia.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:40.730
How do you feel?

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.230
It's so lukewarm and gross...

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.570
I-It's leftover from my lunch.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:48.150
Don't worry. It's not expired or anything.

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:48.780
Probably...

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:49.360
Uh huh...

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:52.320
Thank goodness... we can still talk normally.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:53.570
Hey...

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:58.740
Before, you kept badgering me if I really, really liked you, right?

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:02.580
W-Well... I wouldn't call it "badgering"...

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:04.170
You were quite the badger.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.420
Let me ask you back.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.630
Do you really, really like someone like me?

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.390
You have to hesitate to answer, right?

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.970
Are you sure you don't just feel the same way I do?

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.610
Hey, I'm pretty hungry.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.440
Wanna go get something sweet to eat?

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:28.820
Huh?

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.780
Ah, Takeuchi-kun.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:33.400
I don't usually see you around here.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.110
Out shopping?

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.120
Ah, I get it. Asahi Middle School is around here.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.660
This is our haunt.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:40.580
Then that means Yano hangs out here, too?

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.000
He might be here now.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:42.620
Wanna take a look inside?

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.080
This is pretty good.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.130
Ah, he's here!

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:50.000
Make room for two more.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.090
Huh? Who are they?

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:54.180
That girl's my class president.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:55.260
Class president?

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.850
She must be pretty smart.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.850
Yeah. Especially in math.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:00.970
Oh, really?

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:02.230
She's scary.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.440
Hey, I heard you're in the same class as Yamamoto Yuri?

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:07.810
Ah, yeah.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:10.190
She must be so dark and annoying.

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:12.490
Yeah, she's nothing like her older sister, huh?

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:14.820
Not only is she antisocial, but she's so creepy, too...

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.240
It must be an inferiority complex or something.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.580
After all, those two have always been compared to each other.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:21.330
How can you say that?

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.910
What do you mean?

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:27.500
You don't know anything about her. You just judge her by her looks. Quit it.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:31.090
Huh? We were in the same class for three years of middle school.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.710
I think we'd know more about her than you.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:38.430
Oh? You knew her for three years, but those are the only things you can say about her?

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.010
You don't know anything yourself.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:44.730
She can't even leave messages for people correctly...

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:48.600
That's why Motoharu and Nana-san got into a fight.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:49.980
If they hadn't fought...

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:53.690
...they would've been together that summer vacation, and what happened would--

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:55.320
Stop it.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:58.950
That's not something to talk about here.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.830
Ah... s-sorry.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.910
Why are you guys getting so serious all of a sudden?

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.750
Oh, it's my fault!

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:10.500
I won't forgive anyone who badmouths Nana-san.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.960
Ah... and about Yamamoto's little sister...

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:16.840
She's... yeah, she's fine just the way she is.

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.680
She's not as bad as you all say.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.890
Also, Takahashi Nana.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:25.220
This isn't homeroom, so quit acting like the class president. It's annoying.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:29.440
Die, you jerk!

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:33.860
What was up with that?

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:46.410
I dropped my wallet...

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:47.960
Darn it!

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:58.510
Your wallet.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.970
You're the first girl who's ever told me to die.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.020
Then let me say some more!

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.060
Moron! Idiot! Jackass! Son of a bitch!

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:10.940
Give it back!

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:18.950
You can only see Nana-san in your eyes, anyway...

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:33.580
"Moron, idiot, jackass", huh?

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.300
And my mother isn't a bitch...

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:40.130
She's...

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:43.140
...a prostitute.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:48.020
And my girlfriend was a cheat.

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:54.360
Rea--

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:56.480
She was with another guy when she died in the accident.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:11:59.990
It was her previous boyfriend.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:08.410
They were never through with each another...

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:17.340
Just kidding.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.920
I actually don't know if that was really true.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:22.680
Though, I don't really want to.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:28.890
But if there's one thing I know for sure, it's this.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:33.980
If she ever felt that she wanted to see another guy, then...

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:38.940
...it must partially be my fault for making her feel that way.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:42.530
I'll take you home.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.950
I... can't find any words...

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:49.830
Ah, I'm getting a text message.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.370
"Where are you and what are you doing?"

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:59.250
I'm... taking... Takahashi... san... home.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:02.050
Ah... you don't have to take me home.

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.930
You don't have to, so why don't we go to a pho--

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:06.680
Pho...?

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.850
Why don't we go get our picture taken at photo booth together?

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:14.390
I'm such an idiot, asking at a time like this. Such a total idiot...

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:16.650
Wouldn't one that takes our whole picture be better?

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.020
No... not one of these.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:21.230
I really feels like it's been forever since I've been in one of these.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:24.700
Yano's... smiling.

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.240
Actually, when I think about it... he's always smiling.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.700
Yano, you're really strong, aren't you?

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:33.700
Normally, a person can't say the sorts of things you just told me...

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:35.040
I'm going to press the "confirm" button!

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:37.710
Ah, I thought so. This one's no good.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.000
You're like the woman of 1,000 masks! It's hilarious!

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:45.930
And... I think it's a lot easier to place the blame on yourself than someone else.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.220
Huh? Not the other way around?

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:48.180
Let's do this!

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:50.430
Isn't it easier to blame someone else?

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:54.640
If you blame someone else, you'll just get stubborn and say you'll never forgive them.

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:58.400
But when you blame yourself, you can shrug it off since there's nothing you can do about it.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.400
And you won't get angry that way, either.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:01.480
It's easier.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:05.360
Basically, I'm not being fair.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.910
I pressed the "confirm" button, by the way.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:12.790
Look at the dork! Look at your head!

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.660
I look like a guy...
Look at the dork! Look at your head!

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:18.170
And not only that... my head's bigger than his.

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:20.380
I look like some octopus alien or something...

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.250
Yeah. It's cute.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.630
Cute...? As an octopus...?

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.130
Here's the bus.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:27.260
Bye, then.

00:14:55.500 --> 00:15:00.370
Everyone, we decided what we'll be doing for the school festival at the last committee meeting.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:04.880
Unfortunately, due to the large number of classes doing cafés, we weren't able to do one. Instead...

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:08.880
Our third choice, a short play, won in the ballot!

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.350
What do you mean "our third choice" won?! "Our"?!

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:15.100
Takahashi, were you asleep when we voted?!

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:17.180
It's because I suck at rock-paper-scissors...

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:18.980
But there's a problem. isn't there?

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:21.690
Since you borrow a classroom instead of the auditorium for those...

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:25.360
...only the student judges and teachers will come to see it, right?

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:26.400
It's just too lame...

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:27.400
I have no motivation.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:33.280
I figured that, so I thought about what I could do to increase the audience...

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:35.410
...and I came up with the perfect idea!

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:36.790
And it's...!

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:41.620
How's that sound?

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:43.670
That'll bring them in!

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:45.090
That'll get all the girls here!

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:45.880
Let's do it!

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.880
Yano, I'm gonna decide what play to do today. What do you wanna do?

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:51.590
Don't ask me. Do whatever the heck you want.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:54.100
Y-You don't have to get so mad.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:56.100
Do I always have to clean up your mess?

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:57.850
Clean up my mess...?

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:59.560
What are you gonna do?

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:03.730
I... I was thinking of being the costume director...

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:04.940
It must be so nice to always take the easy way out.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:08.570
Sometimes... you can really be a bastard.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:12.240
So whenever someone does something inconvenient for you, he's a bastard. I see.

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:19.620
You're just mad about before, aren't you? It's true that I was a little hasty, but...

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.910
I guess I don't have a good eye for these sorts of things.

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:23.500
What I said before was a mistake!

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.080
What are you talking about again?

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.340
This little...

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:31.590
W-When I said I liked you, I was wrong!

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:36.140
Told you so.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:50.740
I... just... don't get it anymore.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.700
Ah, how should I put this?

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.910
Do either of you have any stories involving murder?! One that really lets the main character have it?!

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.950
Love stories are out of the question!

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:03.920
I could kill him! I could just kill him!

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:06.920
Damn it! I'll draw a mustache on this devil! Yes! A mustache!

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:09.750
Takahashi-san.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:10.760
Yes?!

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:15.130
There's a student council meeting during lunch tomorrow.

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:16.930
They said they'll assign the classrooms for the festival.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.680
I-Is that so? Thanks.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:24.020
Hey.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.520
Ah, Takeuchi-kun.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:27.610
Sorry about the other day.

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:29.070
What do you mean?

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:30.780
Even though you all got together...

00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:34.240
Ah... that's a daily thing for them.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:36.030
They all have big mouths.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:38.120
That aside, I heard your class is putting on a play?

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:40.120
Yeah. It's really a pain in the neck.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.950
No thanks to him, either.

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:42.870
Him?

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:43.750
Yano, that douchebag!

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:47.500
Did he do something?

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:51.380
Let's not talk about him. My mouth will rot.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:54.300
He must've done something to really annoy you, huh?

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:59.140
Yeah! Sometimes he's so cold, it's hard to believe his blood is flowing!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:03.020
He doesn't even think of others! He could be a little more sensitive!

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:05.230
The complete opposite of you, huh?

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:11.400
Even though I'm really trying my hardest, I get nothing in return...

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.570
When I feel like that, it really aggravates me to see people like him...

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:15.490
He's the worst?

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.200
He's worse than that!

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:24.000
But... people will still come.

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:30.420
Because of Yano, everyone was cool with the play.

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:32.250
You know that type of person, right?

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:38.260
The one who brings a soccer ball to recess, so all of the other kids cheer and go to the field to play.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.010
And when that type of person leaves...

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:44.430
...everyone just gets bored and quits playing. The type who really has a strong presence.

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:48.060
He's one of those types, and I...

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:50.690
...really...

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:54.400
...admire that part of him.

00:18:55.900 --> 00:19:00.700
Just kidding! If I talk about that moron any more, not only will my mouth rot, but so will my brain!

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:01.660
Bye!

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.330
So, what do you think of that?

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.290
What do you mean?

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:20.970
From that day forward, we were really busy looking for a good script...

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:25.930
...and we had no idea of the incredible thing that would happen two days later.

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:29.560
Huh...? Our... our...

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:32.770
...our class has no classroom for the festival.

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:38.110
There's a student council meeting during lunch tomorrow.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:39.900
They said they'll assign the classrooms for the festival.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:42.110
I forgot about it...

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:45.540
I heard our class might not be able to put on a play after all.

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:47.950
Seriously?! That doesn't bother me one bit!

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:48.910
Why, why?

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:52.830
I heard Takahashi forgot to go to the room assignment meeting, so we couldn't get a classroom.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:58.090
We're not completely out of a classroom yet.

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:00.880
There are still open classrooms in the third building.

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:03.470
The third building? That's totally far away from everything!

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:05.850
Nobody would come to that run-down building, anyway!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.350
I just can't get into this anymore.

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:08.430
What was that girl doing?

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:13.400
It's not Nana's fault! I heard the person deciding who goes where forgot about our class.

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:16.650
Nana tried her hardest to protest, but she was told it was too late to move things around.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:21.990
They didn't listen to her at all... they said it was her fault for missing the assignment meeting.

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:25.660
Takahashi.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:26.910
When's the meeting today?

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:31.000
It should've just ended...

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.080
You think some people will still be around?

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:33.960
Probably.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:34.790
I'll go.

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:35.540
But...!

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:39.170
It'll be fine. If anything happens, I'll take responsibility.

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:45.970
You don't have to worry about a thing.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.640
About the classroom distribution...

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:59.150
Yano and I... are different.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:03.400
What? I'm telling you, it's already been decided. Just use one of the leftover rooms.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:03.950
I'm telling you the leftovers are no good, so change it.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:08.530
Yano has a different way of thinking than most people...

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:14.790
I wonder when I began getting that feeling from him...

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:18.540
Even though he's totally irresponsible, he's serious.

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:22.380
Even though he cuts corners, he's confident.

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:28.050
The first school building was impossible to get, but...

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:43.990
Why do you keep... contradicting yourself, Yano?

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:48.740
I thought... you weren't going to clean up after my messes anymore.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:22:00.920
In the end, I'm just too full of pride, too weak-minded, everyone's "friend"...

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:03.630
...have too strong a sense of responsibility, not reliable in the least...

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:05.590
...and just a timid coward...

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:07.090
What's up with that?

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:08.470
They all mean someone who's too softhearted!

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:13.390
I have no eye for anything... I confess my love too quickly... I rely on people too much...

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:14.430
In other words, a...

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:15.060
Moron?

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:16.480
Yeah...

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:19.020
I'm not trying to put on a comic skit here!

00:22:21.190 --> 00:22:24.190
I don't think that's so bad, though.

00:22:24.190 --> 00:22:24.940
What's not?

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:26.570
Being softhearted.

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:27.700
And...

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:32.370
I don't think confessing...

00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:34.500
...was the mistake you're making it out to be.

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:43.880
What...do you mean by that?

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:45.720
Huh? Who knows?

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:53.850
Why do you always evade the important questions by saying things like "who knows?" or "I dunno"?

00:22:53.850 --> 00:22:55.980
I don't.

00:22:55.980 --> 00:22:59.190
You can call it irresponsible or whatever.

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:03.190
You can call it whatever you want, but...

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:06.940
But?

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:09.200
But...

00:23:09.740 --> 00:23:14.160
Aren't I all right the way I am, not knowing?

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:17.660
There he goes...

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:20.250
He's saying it again...

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:21.880
He's contradicting himself again...

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:24.880
But...

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:30.680
Yeah... he might just be all right the way he is...
